      "text": "To find the value of \\( (1 + r)(1 + s)(1 + t) \\), we start by noting that \\( r, s, \\) and \\( t \\) are the roots of the polynomial \\( x^3 - 20x^2 + 18x - 7 = 0 \\). Using Vieta's formulas, we know the following relationships among the roots:\n\n1. \\( r + s + t = 20 \\)\n2. \\( rs + rt + st = 18 \\)\n3. \\( rst = 7 \\)\n\nWe want to find \\( (1 + r)(1 + s)(1 + t) \\). First, we expand the product:\n\n\\[\n(1 + r)(1 + s)(1 + t) = 1 + (r + s + t) + (rs + rt + st) + rst\n\\]\n\nBy substituting the values from Vieta's formulas, we get:\n\n\\[\n(1 + r)(1 + s)(1 + t) = 1 + 20 + 18 + 7\n\\]\n\nSimplifying the right-hand side, we find:\n\n\\[\n1 + 20 + 18 + 7 = 46\n\\]\n\nThus, the value of \\( (1 + r)(1 + s)(1 + t) \\) is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{46}\n\\]",
