      "text": "Given the polynomial \\(x^3 - 20x^2 + 18x - 7 = 0\\), we know that \\(r, s, t\\) are the roots. By Vieta's formulas, we have:\n\n1. \\( r + s + t = 20 \\)\n2. \\( rs + rt + st = 18 \\)\n3. \\( rst = 7 \\)\n\nWe aim to find \\((1+r)(1+s)(1+t)\\). First, expand the expression:\n\n\\[\n(1+r)(1+s)(1+t)\n\\]\n\nSet the product inside the parentheses:\n\n\\[\n1+r + s + t + rs + rt + st + rst\n\\]\n\nAccording to Vieta's formulas, we can substitute the roots' sum, sum of product of roots taken two at a time, and the product of roots. So,\n\n\\[\n(1+r)(1+s)(1+t) = 1 + (r+s+t) + (rs+rt+st) + rst\n\\]\n\nUsing the formulas from Vieta:\n\n\\[\nr + s + t = 20\n\\]\n\\[\nrs + rt + st = 18\n\\]\n\\[\nrst = 7\n\\]\n\nSubstitute these values into the expression:\n\n\\[\n1 + 20 + 18 + 7 = 46\n\\]\n\nHence, the value of \\((1+r)(1+s)(1+t)\\) is \n\n\\[\n\\boxed{46}\n\\]",
